# Patch 0078 — Personal search index (ROADMAP Phase 6; ADR 0012). Full-text
# over the readable text of pages you visit, so universal search can answer
# "where did I find that paper?" — the retrieval backbone the north star's
# knowledge graph and AI features later read.
#
# WHAT: a KavachaIndexer JSWindowActor pair captures the innerText of top-level
# http/https pages (~2.5s after load, capped at 32k chars, never in private
# windows). The parent actor is the policy gate (enabled pref, private-window
# drop, per-tab workspace attribution — same tab layer as ADR 0005) and hands
# off to KavachaPersonalIndex, a process singleton storing one row per URL in
# kavacha-index.sqlite. Universal search gains a "Page Text" source badged with
# workspace attribution; the Privacy Center gains a Personal Index group
# (status, on/off, "Clear index now").
#
# STORAGE — LIKE, not FTS. mozStorage's SQLite ships with NO full-text module
# (fts5/4/3 all fail to create; Firefox strips them, and Places uses frecency +
# LIKE). So search is LIKE with every term required, walking newest-first with
# early termination; ranking (occurrence count, recency tiebreak) and the
# «…» snippet are built in JS. 32k/page keeps the substring scans bounded.
#
# DELETION FOLLOWS PLACES — the privacy contract. The module listens to
# PlacesObservers: history-cleared wipes the index, page-removed drops that URL.
# So "Clear History" and "Forget About This Site" behave as expected with no
# separate chore. Plus: private windows never captured; kavacha.index.enabled
# (unlocked) stops capture; count+age retention (5000 pages / 90 days).
# Local-only; sync waits for Phase 5's E2E story.
#
# NEW DIRECTORY: src/zen/kavacha-index/ needs the src/zen/moz.build DIRS entry
# and a FINAL_TARGET_FILES.actors moz.build; a NEW dir is packaged only by a
# full `mach build` (build-only), not build:ui. DEV-BUILD NOTE: surfer's
# engine symlinks-to-src make the content-process sandbox unable to load the
# actor children (it can't follow the link outside engine/); a packaged build
# (omni.ja, CI) has real content and is unaffected — copy real files into
# engine/zen/kavacha-index/ for local actor testing.
#
# Verified over Marionette on a real build: capture is reliable (3/3 fresh
# pages indexed), LIKE search returns the right page with a JS snippet and
# workspace attribution, re-indexing a URL replaces its text, the enabled pref
# gates capture, and BOTH Places observers fire (page-removed drops one URL,
# history-cleared wipes all).
